/-!
# The cut points of `ptmalloc_init` (PLAN.md G3, malloc)

The 15 cut points: the entry and where two ways meet. From each, the blocks up to the next cut points as one piece
(`W_*`, with its `Sp`, `c_*`): a block's straight-line code, then at its jump's exits the next block's condition, or `Q`
at a cut point or at an offset the proof does not go past (64, 73, 77, 131, 151, 171, 191, 211, 231, 251, 271, 291, 311,
331, 351, 387, 388; the `ret`). `Wt` is the table of the cut points' conditions, `spAll` its `Sp`s, for `Seg.cfg`.
Generated by `tools/blk_gen.py`.
-/
namespace FV7z.Pmi
set_option linter.unusedVariables false
open ZellicX86 Decode FV7z.Leaf

def W_0 (fb : Addr) : Wpt := fun F Wl Q => wp F Wl (o0 fb) (Q 64)
theorem c_0 (prof : Profile) (fb : Addr) : SpF prof pmi pmi_at fb 0 (W_0 fb) :=
  SpF.blkF_then (blk_0 prof fb) (SpF.skip 64)

